{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Using URL Templates when defining tile sources"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"occ","url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/Tile_URL_Templates"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Other Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/Customizing_Fonts","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/Info.plist_Keys","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/GestureRecognizers","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/MultipleImagesExample","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/Predicates_and_Expressions","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/For_Style_Authors"],"anchor":"Other-Articles"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Tile URL Templates","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" objects, specifically "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNRasterTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNVectorTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" objects, can be created using an initializer that accepts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an array of tile URL templates. Tile URL templates are strings that specify the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"URLs of the vector tiles or raster tile images to load. A template resembles an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute URL, but with any number of placeholder strings that the source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evaluates based on the tile it needs to load. For example:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/www.example.com\/tiles\/{z}\/{x}\/{y}.pbf"},{"type":"text","text":" could be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evaluated as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/www.example.com\/tiles\/14\/6\/9.pbf"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/www.example.com\/tiles\/{z}\/{x}\/{y}{ratio}.png"},{"type":"text","text":" could be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"evaluated as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/www.example.com\/tiles\/14\/6\/9@2x.png"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tile URL templates are also used to define tilesets in TileJSON manifests or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/maplibre.org\/maplibre-style-spec\/sources\/#raster","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/maplibre.org\/maplibre-style-spec\/sources\/#vector-tiles","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sources in style JSON files. See the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/mapbox\/tilejson-spec\/tree\/master\/2.2.0","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for information about tile URL templates in the context of a TileJSON or style"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON file."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tile sources support the following placeholder strings in tile URL templates,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all of which are optional:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Placeholder string"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Description"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{x}"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The index of the tile along the map’s x axis according to Spherical Mercator projection. If the value is 0, the tile’s left edge corresponds to the 180th meridian west. If the value is 2^z−1, the tile’s right edge corresponds to the 180th meridian east."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{y}"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The index of the tile along the map’s y axis according to Spherical Mercator projection. If the value is 0, the tile’s tile edge corresponds to arctan(sinh(π)), or approximately 85.0511 degrees north. If the value is 2^z−1, the tile’s bottom edge corresponds to −arctan(sinh(π)), or approximately 85.0511 degrees south. The y axis is inverted if the options parameter contains "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNTileSourceOptionTileCoordinateSystem"},{"type":"text","text":" with a value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNTileCoordinateSystem\/MLNTileCoordinateSystemTMS"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{z}"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tile’s zoom level. At zoom level 0, each tile covers the entire world map; at zoom level 1, it covers ¼ of the world; at zoom level 2, 1⁄16 of the world, and so on. For tiles loaded by a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNRasterTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" object, whether the tile zoom level matches the map’s current zoom level depends on the value of the source’s tile size as specified in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLNTileSourceOptionTileSize"},{"type":"text","text":" key of the options parameter."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{bbox-epsg-3857}"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tile’s bounding box, expressed as a comma-separated list of the tile’s western, southern, eastern, and northern extents according to Spherical Mercator (EPSG:3857) projection. The bounding box is typically used with map services conforming to the "},{"type":"text","text":"Web Map Service"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{quadkey}"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A quadkey indicating both the tile’s location and its zoom level. The quadkey is typically used with "},{"type":"text","text":"Bing Maps"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{ratio}"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A suffix indicating the resolution of the tile image. The suffix is the empty string for standard resolution displays and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@2x"},{"type":"text","text":" for Retina displays, including displays for which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIScreen.scale"},{"type":"text","text":" is 3."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{prefix}"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two hexadecimal digits chosen such that each visible tile has a different prefix. The prefix is typically used for domain sharding."}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more information about the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{x}"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{y}"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{z}"},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder strings,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consult the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/wiki.openstreetmap.org\/wiki\/Slippy_map_tilenames","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/tile_url_templates"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/Info.plist_Keys":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/info.plist_keys","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"MapLibre Native for iOS supports custom "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Info.plist"},{"type":"text","text":" keys in your application in order to configure various settings."}],"title":"Info.plist Keys","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/Info.plist_Keys","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Powerful, free and open-source mapping toolkit with full control over data sources and styling."}],"title":"MapLibre","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/For_Style_Authors":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/for_style_authors","abstract":[],"title":"Information for Style Authors","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/For_Style_Authors","role":"article","type":"topic"},"https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Slippy_map_tilenames":{"identifier":"https:\/\/wiki.openstreetmap.org\/wiki\/Slippy_map_tilenames","type":"link","title":"OpenStreetMap Wiki","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenStreetMap Wiki"}],"url":"https:\/\/wiki.openstreetmap.org\/wiki\/Slippy_map_tilenames"},"https://maplibre.org/maplibre-style-spec/sources/#vector-tiles":{"identifier":"https:\/\/maplibre.org\/maplibre-style-spec\/sources\/#vector-tiles","type":"link","title":"vector","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"vector","type":"codeVoice"}],"url":"https:\/\/maplibre.org\